    "result_text": "There's exactly one test class and all tests are green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) on the owner resource:\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new helper in `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 computes the segment: `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`; `METRO` when the locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD) else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment`, deriving locality from the owner's `customerCode` (consistent with the existing `locality`/`timezone` mappings) and passing `membershipLevel`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it into the JSON response.\n\nThe build regenerates `OwnerDto` from the spec, and both acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, along with the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
